F436|THE SINK IS THE AMDAHL BOTTLENECK AND THE IDLE-FILL MECHANISM IS GATED OFF DURING IT|READOUT of F435, which was FALSIFIED by its own falsifier: replanned fired exactly ONCE in each 3-node cell, round 0, adding 2 to 4 tasks, stopped false - and ZERO times in the 1-node cell, which is correct because one node with two slots rarely has idle_capacity >= 2. So the mechanism RUNS and the defect is downstream, exactly as the falsifier said it would be. WHERE THE IDLE TIME ACTUALLY IS, measured second-by-second over each dispatch window by pairing task_dispatched with task_completed and testing whether integrate-verify was in flight: baseline-n3-r0 sink 56.2 of 106 min (53.1 percent of the window) with 100 PERCENT OF THAT SINK TIME AT 2 OR FEWER CONCURRENT TASKS out of 6 slots. n3-r1 sink 45.0 of 74 min (60.6 percent), 29.7 min of it at or under 2. n3-r2 30.7 percent. n3-r3 15.6 percent, 100 percent of it at or under 2. IN THE BEST CELL EVER RECORDED, MORE THAN HALF THE EXECUTE WINDOW IS ONE SERIAL TASK WITH FOUR OF SIX SLOTS EMPTY. AND THE GATE IS EXPLICIT: the dynamic-replan trigger at scheduler.rs 2321 requires NOT sink_in_flight, so the one mechanism built to fill idle slots is forbidden during the longest idle window in the run. THE SECOND HALF OF THE SAME BOTTLENECK IS THE PREFIX: the window before the first dispatch is 2382s on the 1-node cell versus 2038, 1863, 1316, 2883 on the 3-node cells, mean 2025s - THREE TIMES THE HARDWARE BUYS 15 PERCENT - and it is 21 to 38 percent of every run. Together the prefix and the sink account for most of a run and neither scales with the fleet. ⚠️ THE GATE IS DEFENSIBLE AND I AM NOT CALLING IT A BUG: integrate-verify is the join that reconciles cross-module interfaces, and injecting new build work mid-join could invalidate it. ⚠️ CONFIDENCE STATEMENT, EXPLICIT: I am NOT confident I can safely restructure or sub-shard the sink - getting it wrong breaks the one phase that makes modules agree - and I will not ship a change there